From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jay Leaton <58495321+jayleaton@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:17:34 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 049/207] dsv41: engine-native compute lane (opt-in
 TF_DSV41_COMPUTE_LANE)

A request that lists {"type": "code_interpreter"} gets a built-in python
tool. Its reply holds at each EOS (Request.hold_eos): the stream keeps its
slot and KV, and the engine skips it while the server runs the calls in the
sandboxed executor. The server renders the template's tool-result turn and
resumes the stream with those tokens as forced verify rows, so the model
continues with the same ids a client round trip would send, without
re-prefilling.

- lanes: hold_eos/held on Stream, a held EOS stays pending (window cut),
  hold.resumeHeld, runnableCount for the idle checks
- lane host: resume_held queued like cancel and applied on the engine
  thread; at most one resume a hold
- server: Generation moved to generation.zig; compute_turns (opt-in,
  arming, client stream filter) and compute_segments (segment loop, result
  insertion, merged reply with tensorfold.compute)
- serve: __compute_sandbox trampoline entry in main

Flag unset: no pool, hold_eos never set, D's behaviour unchanged.
